Act as a Senior Full-Stack Developer & Mobile App Architect. Build a cross-platform (Android, iOS, Web) Quran Learning Application based on the "Tamyiz" method (word-by-word grammar, color-coded categories, and interactive quizzes) with a monthly subscription system of IDR 10,000/month.

### 1. TECH STACK & ARCHITECTURE
- Frontend: Flutter or React Native (Expo) - Single codebase for Mobile (Android/iOS) and Web (PWA).
- Backend & Database: Supabase (Use Free Tier specs: PostgreSQL, Authentication, Storage, Row Level Security).
- Admin Panel: Web-based Admin Dashboard (integrated into the web frontend or separate route like /admin).
- Payment Integration: Midtrans / Xendit (QRIS, E-Wallet, Transfer Bank) for Web, and In-App Purchase (Google Play & Apple IAP) for Mobile.

### 2. CORE FEATURES & DATABASE SCHEMA
Create the following database tables in Supabase with RLS (Row Level Security) enabled:
- `users`: id, email, full_name, role (enum: 'user', 'admin'), created_at.
- `subscriptions`: id, user_id, status (enum: 'active', 'inactive', 'expired'), start_date, end_date, payment_method, updated_at.
- `quran_words`: id, surah_number, ayah_number, word_position, arabic_text, translation, tamyiz_category (Isim, Fi'il, Huruf, Tamyiz 1-4), color_code, audio_url.
- `lessons`: id, title, level, category, description, order_index.
- `quizzes`: id, lesson_id, question, options (JSON), correct_answer, score_points.
- `user_progress`: id, user_id, lesson_id, is_completed, score, updated_at.

### 3. SUBSCRIPTION & PAYMENT FLOW (IDR 10,000/month)
- Implement active subscription checks middleware/guard for locked content.
- Non-subscribed users can only access Lesson 1 (Free Trial).
- Subscribed users get full access to all lessons and quizzes.
- Web version integrates local payment gateway (Midtrans/Xendit) supporting QRIS and GoPay/OVO for IDR 10,000/month.
- Automatically update `subscriptions` table upon successful payment webhook payload.

### 4. CONTENT SECURITY & ANTI-PIRACY (CRITICAL)
- Do NOT hardcode Quran text or audio locally in the app bundle. All data must be fetched dynamically from Supabase API using authorization tokens.
- Secure media files: Store audio/video in private Supabase Storage buckets, accessed strictly via short-lived Signed URLs or HLS streaming.
- Web Protection: Disable right-click, disable Developer Tools shortcuts (F12, Ctrl+Shift+I), and suppress video/audio direct download buttons.
- Mobile App Protection: Enable screen protection (FLAG_SECURE on Android, iOS screen recording preventer) to block screenshotting and screen recording on lesson pages.

### 5. ADMIN DASHBOARD ROUTE (/admin)
- Accessible only by users with `role = 'admin'`.
- Analytics Overview: Total active subscribers, total revenue monthly, daily active learners.
- User Management: View user list, search users, manually activate/deactivate subscription status (for manual payments/testing).
- Content Management (CMS): CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete) for lessons, Quran word data, color codes, and quiz questions.

### 6. UI/UX REQUIREMENTS
- Clean, modern, and mobile-friendly UI layout.
- High-contrast color coding for Tamyiz grammar categories (e.g., Isim = Blue, Fi'il = Red, Huruf = Green).
- Interactive quiz interface with immediate feedback, progress bar, and score summary.
- Seamless authentication flow (Email/Password & Google Sign-In).

